cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite them as below."
title: "Validating generated segmentation variability for radiomic feature selection: code and results"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nerdgerd/segmentation-measurement-validation"
abstract: >-
  Code, locked specifications and feature-level results for the study
  "Validating generated segmentation variability for radiomic feature selection:
  correlation, scale and decision agreement". The study compares generated with
  original-versus-corrected contour variability for 192 geometric MRI features in
  147 UPENN-GBM and 97 BraTS-TCGA-GBM patients: the correlation of CCC values
  against a simulated correlation baseline, the magnitude of feature differences
  and feature selection at five CCC thresholds.
keywords:
  - radiomics
  - feature robustness
  - segmentation variability
  - contour perturbation
  - glioblastoma
  - concordance correlation coefficient
  - feature selection
